---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_UPDATED_EN, mailto, PUBLISHER } from '../../lib/legal';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" lang="en" description="KareTakvim privacy policy: no account, no location, notes stay on your device.">
  <main id="main" class="prose">
    <article class="prose-card legal">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: {LEGAL_UPDATED_EN} · <a href="/gizlilik" hreflang="tr" lang="tr">Türkçe</a></p>
      <p class="lead">In short: KareTakvim does not require an account, does not ask for your location and does not use advertising or tracking. Your notes stay on your device.</p>
      <p>This policy covers the KareTakvim mobile app (iOS and Android), its widgets and the KareTakvim website. The service is provided by {PUBLISHER}. The Turkish version is the governing text.</p>

      <h2>Data that stays on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Notes</strong> you write for a day are saved only on your device (a local database in the app, the browser's localStorage on the website). They are never sent to a server, never synced and never shown in widgets.</li>
        <li><strong>Selected city</strong> is stored on your device. Sunrise and sunset times are calculated on the device from the province centre's coordinates. No GPS or device location is requested.</li>
        <li><strong>Content cache</strong>: public daily content you have viewed is cached on your device for offline use.</li>
        <li><strong>Widget data</strong>: today's date, public event title and sun times are shared between the app and its widget on your device. Notes are never included.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If your device's own backup (iCloud or Google backup) is enabled, the operating system may include app data in that backup, which belongs to your Apple or Google account. We have no access to it.</p>

      <h2>Network requests</h2>
      <p>Daily content (notable day, on-this-day event, quote of the day) is fetched read-only from a public content service hosted on Supabase. Requests contain only the dates requested — no notes, city or identifiers. As with any internet request, your IP address and device/browser information are technically visible to the hosting providers and may appear briefly in their security and operations logs. We do not use these logs to identify, profile or advertise to you. Tapping a "source" link opens an external website, whose own privacy policy applies.</p>

      <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No account, name, email or phone number.</li>
        <li>No location, contacts, photos, microphone or camera access.</li>
        <li>No advertising, advertising identifiers (IDFA/AAID) or cross-app tracking.</li>
        <li>No analytics, usage measurement or crash reporting SDKs.</li>
        <li>No cookies on the website.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
      <p>Delete a single note with the "Sil" (Delete) link on the page. Uninstalling the app removes all of its data; clearing site data in your browser removes website data. Since there are no accounts and notes never reach us, we hold no personal data to delete.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>KareTakvim is a general-audience calendar. We do not knowingly collect personal data from anyone, including children.</p>

      <h2>Your rights (KVKK / GDPR)</h2>
      <p>Under Turkish Law No. 6698 (KVKK) and, where applicable, the GDPR, you may ask whether any personal data about you is processed and request access, correction, deletion or object to processing. We will respond within 30 days.</p>

      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>Any change will be published on this page with a new "Last updated" date.</p>
      {
        CONTACT_EMAIL ? (
          <p>Contact: <a href={mailto('KareTakvim privacy')}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a></p>
        ) : (
          <p>Contact: see the <a href="/iletisim">contact page</a>.</p>
        )
      }
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
